          "description": "Reads content from internal Amazon websites (amazon.com amazon.dev a2z.com aws.dev TLDs)\n### User Alias Handling\n\nThe terms alias and login are synonyms\n<Rule>Many payloads may contain an alias/user handle of an employee. ALWAYS use phonetool.amazon.com to lookup a real name from an alias IF necessary, NEVER guess a name from an alias based on alias appearance</Rule>\n<CurrentUserAmazonAlias value=\"earaghbi\" />\n### Ticket Severity\nTickets at Amazon have severity SEV from 1-5, 1 and 2 are most severe and page resolvers 2.5 - business hours sev 2 3 – Group productivity impaired 4 – Individual productivity impaired 5 – Productivity not immediately affected\n\n### Website Details\nbroadcast.amazon.com internal videos, transcripts for company communications and events\nprod.artifactbrowser.brazil.aws.dev Brazil artifacts, ?include-toc=true will include table of contents\ncloudscape.aws.dev Cloudscape design system documentation: components, patterns, guidelines for building AWS products and experiences\nmeridian.a2z.com Meridian design system documentation: components, guides, patterns, etc Version selection via ?version=VERSION - default 8.x\ndesign-inspector.a2z.com design diagrams and threat models in DrawIO format\nmcm.amazon.dev manual change management checklists which can be in progress/approved/pending with comments and approvals\noncall.corp.amazon.com oncall rotations and current oncall\nphonetool.amazon.com employee roster including manager, directs, level, job title, name, person & employee id, building code\napollo.amazon.com distributed deployment orchestration system managing interactions between application code and infra (NOT to be confused with Apollo the building!)\nw.amazon.com internal MediaWiki instance for Amazon /bin/owner/PATH will fetch owner info for /bin/view/PATH\ntaskei.amazon.dev task and project management, sprints, kanban boards, planning and scrum processes\nsim.amazon.com and issues.amazon.com are older