          "description": "Read content from internal Amazon websites.\n\nSupported websites and their purposes:\n\nDocumentation & Knowledge:\n- docs.hub.amazon.dev: Internal technical documentation\n- hub.cx.aws.dev: Internal technical documentation for building an experience in the AWS Management Console\n- btdocs.builder-tools.aws.dev: BuilderHub contributor documentation\n- docs.ctps.amazon.dev: CTPS technical documentation\n- docs.paystation.amazon.dev: PayStation technical documentation\n- skb.highcastle.a2z: Security knowledge base docs\n- aristotle.a2z.com: AWS Security Knowledge Base Docs\n- docs.aws.amazon.com: External AWS documentation\n- documentation.skynet.aws.dev: Skynet documentation\n- sage.amazon.dev: Engineering Q&A platform\n- datacentral.a2z.com/cradle: DataCentral Cradle job runs\n- oldfart.tools.amazon.dev: Important user tenure information and cohort statistics\n- sidekick.aka.amazon.com: Help users perform redundant tasks of aggregating trouble ticket or SIM data by creating custom oncall reports\n- grass.integ.amazon.com, grass-na.aka.amazon.com, grass-eu.aka.amazon.com, grass-fe.aka.amazon.com, grass-cn.aka.amazon.com: Grass Portal for exploring Ordering data, purchase/order/shipment content, and annotations\n- docs.corp.asic.blink.devices.a2z.com: RBKS ASIC Documentation\n\nDocument Storage & Sharing:\n- workdocs.amazon.com: Amazon WorkDocs (PDFs, Word Docs, Excel)\n- drive-render.corp.amazon.com: Amazon Drive content\n- quip-amazon.com: Collaborative documents\n- paste.amazon.com: Raw content sharing\n- w.amazon.com: Internal MediaWiki\n- noogle-eu.amazon.com: Noogle EU customer information system\n- noogle-na.amazon.com: Noogle NA customer information system\n- noogle-fe.amazon.com: Noogle FE customer information system\n- apttool.amazon.com: Weblab APT report\n- confluence.collab.games.aws.dev: Amazon Games internal confluence page\n\nDevelopment & Build Tools:\n- code.amazon.com: Internal code repository\n- build.amazon.com: Build fl